SET
  @Name_ff9802e995a7 = N'Claude Opus 5.5'
SET
  @Description_ff9802e995a7 = N'Anthropic''s Opus-class flagship, released September 22, 2026 as the successor to Claude Opus 5 and now Anthropic''s recommended default for most workloads. Built for long-running agentic coding and knowledge work; Anthropic positions it as matching Claude Fable 5.1 on most tasks at lower cost and lower latency. 1M-token context included at standard pricing, 128K max output (300K on the Batches API with the output-300k-2026-03-24 beta header), adaptive thinking always on with an effort setting that defaults to medium (versus high on Fable 5.1 and Sonnet 5). Supports structured outputs (JSON schema via response_format), strict tool use, streaming and vision. Per-token price is $4/$20 per 1M - 20% below the $5/$25 shared by Opus 5, 4.8, 4.7, 4.6 and 4.5 - and cache hits are $0.20/1M, a 0.05x base-input multiplier that sits between Fable 5.1''s 0.025x and the standard 0.1x. Anthropic reports ~40% lower cost on typical workloads, attributing part of that to fewer tokens and fewer turns rather than the rate alone. Uses the Claude 4.7-and-later tokenizer (~30% more tokens for the same text than Sonnet 4.6 and earlier). Available on the Claude API, Claude Platform on AWS, Amazon Bedrock (anthropic.claude-opus-5-5), Google Cloud Vertex AI and Microsoft Foundry (both claude-opus-5-5); only the Claude API, Bedrock and OpenRouter routes are modelled here. Fast mode (research preview, Claude API only) serves this model at a $8/$40 premium and is not modelled as a separate record. Tentative retirement not sooner than September 22, 2027.'
SET
